# Line endings for the statusline installer wrappers.
#
# Pinned here rather than left to each contributor's core.autocrlf: a committer
# on Windows without autocrlf would otherwise commit a CRLF install.sh, which
# fails on Linux/macOS with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M". Git Bash
# happens to tolerate CRLF, so the breakage would only show up for other people.
*.sh  text eol=lf

# The mirror case — cmd.exe and PowerShell are conventionally CRLF on Windows.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
